<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<OutputType>Library</OutputType>
		<DockerDefaultTargetOS>Linux</DockerDefaultTargetOS>

		<GeneratePackageOnBuild>true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
		<PackageId>CoreSystem.Cache</PackageId>
		<Version>3.0.0</Version>
		<AssemblyVersion>3.0.0</AssemblyVersion>
		<FileVersion>3.0.0.0</FileVersion>
		<InformationalVersion>3.0.0</InformationalVersion>
		<Authors>Federin Pastor Gutierrez Ortiz</Authors>
		<Description>Production-ready cache abstraction for .NET 8 with In-Memory caching, extensible external storage, tag-based invalidation, HTTP response caching, and OpenTelemetry metrics.</Description>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/FEDERIN/CoreSystem.Cache</RepositoryUrl>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://federin.github.io/CoreSystem.Cache</PackageProjectUrl>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE</PackageLicenseFile>
		<PackageTags>Cache;Caching;DistributedCache;MemoryCache;HTTP;OpenTelemetry;Observability;.NET8</PackageTags>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>3.0.0: BREAKING CHANGES, two of them. (1) CacheOptions.MaxCacheableSize is removed. It was declared with a 1 MB default and copied by CopyFrom, but no cache storage ever read it, and it never did: it shipped dead. It also could not be implemented coherently, because Redis serializes first so a byte length is free, while the Memory provider stores the live object and never serializes, so measuring it would mean serializing every value purely to inspect it on the fastest path. A limit that binds for Redis users and silently does nothing for Memory users is a worse trap than no limit at all. Entries of any size are cached. Configure HTTP lifetime with DefaultExpiration and CacheableAttribute; for bounding memory use IMemoryCache.SizeLimit on the Memory provider or maxmemory-policy on the Redis server. (2) ICacheTagIndex&lt;T&gt;, MemoryKeyTracker and DefaultRequestCachePolicy are now internal. All three were public while the contract they implement is internal, so no consumer could substitute or implement them; a public type whose only interfaces are internal is not an extension point, only a wider API surface. ICacheTagIndex&lt;T&gt; was the last public member of Storage/Abstractions, and DefaultRequestCachePolicy now matches its sibling DefaultResponseCachePolicy, already internal sealed. The seams behind them are unchanged. MIGRATION: delete any assignment to MaxCacheableSize; reference IExternalCacheStorage instead of ICacheTagIndex&lt;T&gt;; remove any direct use of MemoryKeyTracker or DefaultRequestCachePolicy, all three being wired by the library at registration time. Nothing else changed. Dependency injection, the cache pipeline, Redis and Rehydration are unaffected, so 3.0.0 of CoreSystem.Cache.Redis and CoreSystem.Cache.Rehydration are released only to move their dependency onto this version.</PackageReleaseNotes>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="CoreSystem.Http" />
		<PackageReference Include="CoreSystem.Memory" />
		<PackageReference Include="CoreSystem.Resilience" />
		<PackageReference Include="CoreSystem.Serialization" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
		<None Include="CHANGELOG.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
		<None Include="..\..\LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
    	<FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App" />
	</ItemGroup>
	
	<ItemGroup>
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="Core.Cache.Redis" />
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="Core.Cache.Rehydration" />
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="Core.Cache.Redis.UnitTests" />
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="Core.Cache.Rehydration.UnitTests" />
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="Core.Cache.UnitTests" />
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="Core.Cache.IntegrationTests" />
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="DynamicProxyGenAssembly2" />
	</ItemGroup>

</Project>